OL,3,GNEWSAPorts calls for responsible
OL,4,Afishing around harbour
OL,5,
OL,6,FIslanders are being asked to use the
OL,7,Fharbour responsibly after a spate of
OL,8,Fincidents involving fishing equipment,
OL,9,Fproperty damage and wildlife.
OL,11,FGuernsey Ports and local angling clubs
OL,12,Fsaid while most anglers used the
OL,13,Fharbour responsibly, several recent
OL,14,Fincidents had raised "concerns".
OL,16,FIncidents include young people climbing
OL,17,Fharbour ladders at the Fish Quay, young
OL,18,Fgulls becoming entangled in discarded
OL,19,Ffishing line and hooks, fishing tackle
OL,20,Fgetting caught on vessels, masts and
OL,21,Faerials and fishing lures being found
OL,22,Fin rigging.
OL,23,APub: 19-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Ch Is NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
